CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --show-symbol-table
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*continue not allowed here.*$
^.*break not allowed here.*$
--
Verifies that `break` and `continue` are permitted inside the
body of a range-based `for` loop, per [stmt.ranged].  Without the
fix, CBMC's range-for lowering type-checked the body without
setting `break_is_allowed`/`continue_is_allowed` to true, and
rejected `continue;` (and would also reject `break;`).
